# Which model server the benchmark agent talks to.
#
# Copy to .env in the repository root and edit. The agent CLI
# (agent/harness/agent.py) and the local lifecycle wrapper
# (agent/lifecycle.py) both read it. An exported shell variable wins over
# this file, and a command-line flag wins over both, so .env only supplies what
# you have not set another way. .env is ignored by git, and every key in this
# example is a placeholder: put real keys in your own .env only.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works: the agent speaks that protocol and knows
# nothing else about the server. Uncomment one block.
#
# AGENT_MODEL_SERVER says who owns the endpoint: bundled means the local
# lifecycle wrapper starts and stops the vLLM server in agent/model_server.sh
# around every phase, external means the endpoint is already there and the
# wrapper only chains the phases. agent/lifecycle.py reads it from here,
# locally and in the cluster; the agent CLI itself never starts a server.
#
# AGENT_ENABLE_THINKING pins the served chat template's thinking mode on via
# chat_template_kwargs (vLLM's switch for a hybrid reasoning model such as
# GLM-4.5-Air or Qwen3), instead of relying on the server's own default. Off
# unless set, since an unrelated OpenAI-compatible endpoint (the OpenAI or
# Mistral blocks below) could reject a field it does not recognise. It does
# not force non-empty reasoning on every turn -- a hybrid model may still
# answer some turns with none -- it only asks the template not to suppress it.

# --- Self-hosted vLLM, port-forwarded by agent/model_server.sh (the default) ---
AGENT_MODEL=qwen3.8-27b
AGENT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001/v1
AGENT_API_KEY=EMPTY
# AGENT_ENABLE_THINKING=true

# --- Self-hosted vLLM reached in-cluster (agent Job, no port forward) ---
# AGENT_MODEL=qwen3.8-27b
# AGENT_BASE_URL=http://bexhoma-agent-model/v1
# AGENT_MODEL_SERVER=bundled
# AGENT_API_KEY=EMPTY

# --- Self-hosted vLLM, GLM-4.5-Air (GPTQ INT4) instead of Qwen3.8 ---
# Deploys agent/k8s/vllm-glm45-air-int4.yml in place of the default
# agent/k8s/vllm-qwen38-27b.yml, serving QuantTrio/GLM-4.5-Air-GPTQ-Int4-Int8Mix
# (the smaller REAP-82B-pruned checkpoint's own INT4 quantizations are
# currently unreachable -- see the comments at the top of that manifest).
# ~67GB of weights, so this manifest is pinned to the cluster's H200 node, not
# either Hopper node. --model-server-manifest on agent/lifecycle.py overrides
# this per run. If a server started from the other manifest is already up,
# bring it down first (agent/model_server.sh down / .ps1 down): Kubernetes
# will not change a running pod's container command in place, so `up` alone
# will not switch it.
# AGENT_MODEL=glm-4.5-air-int4
# AGENT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001/v1
# AGENT_API_KEY=EMPTY
# AGENT_ENABLE_THINKING=true
# MODEL_SERVER_MANIFEST=agent/k8s/vllm-glm45-air-int4.yml

# --- Self-hosted vLLM, Llama-3.3-70B (GPTQ INT4) instead of Qwen3.8 ---
# Deploys agent/k8s/vllm-llama33-70b-int4.yml in place of the default
# agent/k8s/vllm-qwen38-27b.yml, serving shuyuej/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct-GPTQ
# (meta-llama's own repo is gated behind a license acceptance this deployment
# cannot complete without a Hugging Face account; this community
# requantization is confirmed public). 42GB of weights, comfortable on either
# Hopper node, but note vLLM's llama3_json tool-call parser only supports one
# tool call per turn, unlike the Qwen and GLM manifests. Same switching rules
# as the GLM block above: --model-server-manifest overrides this per run, and
# a server started from another manifest needs `down` before `up`.
# AGENT_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-int4
# AGENT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001/v1
# AGENT_API_KEY=EMPTY
# MODEL_SERVER_MANIFEST=agent/k8s/vllm-llama33-70b-int4.yml

# Namespace the self-hosted vLLM server is created in and deleted from by
# agent/model_server.sh. Required by the two self-hosted blocks above, and it has
# no default on purpose: the switch also writes it into the kube context, so a
# default would send the model server and every later namespace-less kubectl
# call -- bexhoma's own included -- into whichever account that default named.
# It must equal the namespace declared for this context in cluster.config. The
# in-cluster lifecycle Job takes it from its own namespace and ignores this.
# MODEL_SERVER_NAMESPACE=my-namespace

# --- Local Ollama ---
# Ollama serves the window a tag pins in num_ctx, not the model's architectural
# maximum, and falls back to 4096 tokens for a tag that pins nothing. Runs peak
# near 26k prompt tokens, so use a 64k tag; plain qwen3.5:9b would truncate.
# Uncomment exactly one AGENT_MODEL.
# AGENT_MODEL=qwen3.5:9b-ctx64k   # 9.7B, spills ~38% to CPU, ~9 tok/s
# AGENT_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b-ctx64k   # 4.7B, fits the 8Gi card, ~100 tok/s
# AGENT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# AGENT_MODEL_SERVER=external
# AGENT_API_KEY=ollama

# --- OpenAI ---
# AGENT_MODEL=gpt-4o
# AGENT_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# AGENT_MODEL_SERVER=external
# AGENT_API_KEY=sk-replace-with-your-openai-key

# --- Mistral (OpenAI-compatible endpoint) ---
# AGENT_MODEL=mistral-large-latest
# AGENT_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# AGENT_MODEL_SERVER=external
# AGENT_API_KEY=replace-with-your-mistral-key

# --- OpenRouter, Gemma 4 31B (used when every cluster GPU was taken) ---
# AGENT_EXTRA_BODY pins requests to Crusoe's full-precision (BF16) endpoint and
# turns thinking on through OpenRouter's switch; AGENT_ENABLE_THINKING has no
# effect here. Crusoe accepts the full 65536-token reply ceiling. Novita, the
# other BF16 provider, refused an 18k-token prompt as too long on 2026-09-22,
# so it is not allowed as a fallback.
# AGENT_MODEL=google/gemma-4-31b-it
# AGENT_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# AGENT_MODEL_SERVER=external
# AGENT_API_KEY=replace-with-your-openrouter-key
# AGENT_EXTRA_BODY={"provider": {"order": ["crusoe"], "allow_fallbacks": false, "quantizations": ["bf16"]}, "reasoning": {"enabled": true}}

# --- BHT LLM API (Sophia), hosted by the university, no cluster needed ---
# Serves its models under tier aliases rather than their own names; the alias
# is what goes into AGENT_MODEL. Which tiers a key may use depends on the BHT
# user group it was issued to. All three return proper tool calls. bht/large
# returns its thinking inline as a <think> block in the reply text rather than
# in a separate reasoning field, so that text reaches the transcript as-is.
# The windows below are the limits BHT serves each model with, which can be
# smaller than the model's own. The gateway does not publish them; the agent
# learns each one from the tier's first over-length refusal. bht/medium's 32768
# tokens leave only about 6k for a reply once a run's prompt reaches its usual
# peak near 26k.
# Each tier allows a key 100000 tokens a day, prompt and reply counted together.
# One design phase has used between 280k and 640k tokens, so without a raised
# quota the API suits short tests, not a full investigation; a turn refused for
# quota ends the phase after the agent's few minutes of retries.
# The endpoint also lists mistralai/Mistral-Medium-3.5-128B and
# deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731, but on 2026-09-22 the gateway had no route
# to either (404). Uncomment exactly one AGENT_MODEL.
# AGENT_MODEL=bht/small    # Qwen/Qwen3-14B, 65536-token window
# AGENT_MODEL=bht/medium   # google/gemma-4-31B-it, 32768-token window
#   (BHT's serving limit; the model itself supports 262144 tokens)
# AGENT_MODEL=bht/large    # cyankiwi/MiniMax-M2.7-AWQ-4bit, 196000-token window
# AGENT_BASE_URL=https://sophia-api.bht-berlin.de/v1
# AGENT_MODEL_SERVER=external
# AGENT_API_KEY=replace-with-your-bht-key

# Optional: bexhoma's result folder, otherwise taken from cluster.config.
# AGENT_RESULTS=/path/to/results

# The experiment design handbook, read before every design and every follow-up.
# Empty the value to design without one, which is the other arm of the
# with/without ablation. Both command lines take --method to override this for a
# single run. A path that names no file is rejected, so a typo cannot quietly
# turn a run into the no-handbook arm of the ablation.
AGENT_METHOD=agent/experiment_design_handbook.md

# Whether agent/lifecycle.py also answers the question with the bare model
# first -- no catalog, handbook, or tools -- as a separate investigation, for
# comparison with the full pipeline's answer. On by default; set to 0 (or pass
# --no-baseline) to skip it. The agent CLI's own `--phase baseline` is
# unaffected by this and always available.
AGENT_BASELINE=1

# Optional: shell command that renews cluster credentials. It runs immediately
# before an experiment is handed to the cluster, because a design phase can run
# for hours and a session that was valid at launch is routinely expired by the
# time it submits. A failure or a hang stops the submission instead of leaving a
# benchmark that cannot start. Keep the credentials in the script, not here.
# AGENT_CLUSTER_LOGIN=bash ~/scripts/kube-login.sh && kubectl config set-context my-context --namespace=my-namespace
